## FINDING — enumerated bounds are documented but not proven

`testdata/constraint-enumeration.md` asserts, on all 167 rows, "Enforced exactly
as declared before identity calculation or verification." For the 23 declared
constraints below that claim is not defended by any test: each gate can be
**narrowed by one** and `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1` still
reports `ok`.

This is the exact shape the task's own Definition of Done forbids — "Prove a
bound by NARROWING the gate, not only by deleting it. A delete-only mutant
proves the gate exists and says nothing about the class it covers" — and it is
what makes the audit claim unreproducible: a future edit can widen any of these
with a green suite and a stale artifact row that still says "enforced exactly
as declared".

Each mutant below was applied individually to the candidate; `go test
./internal/canonicaljson -count=1` printed `ok` every time.

### §1.6 common data rules

| # | Widened gate | Mutant that survives | Value the mutant admits |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | reverse-DNS "contains at least one dot" | `reverseDNSPattern` `(\.…)+` → `(\.…)*` | `extensions:{"nodot":true}` (verified accepted under the mutant, refused by the candidate) |
| 2 | migration provenance canonical semver | `semverPattern` → `^([0-9]*)\.([0-9]*)\.([0-9]*)$` | `schema_version:"01.0.0"` |

The existing negative set (`not_namespaced`, `A.b`, `1a.b`, `a..b`, `.a`,
`a.b_`, 64-char label, over-253) never isolates the dot clause: `not_namespaced`
also carries an underscore, so it fails on the character class instead.

### §5.1 Session Record / Launch Plan / Task-board Reference

| # | Widened gate | Mutant that survives |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 3 | `argv` array `[1..128]` | `requireArray(object,"argv",128)` → `129` |
| 4 | encoded `argv` ≤ 65,536 bytes | `len(encodedArgv) > 65_536` → `65_537` |
| 5 | `env_names` `[0..64]` | `requireArray(object,"env_names",64)` → `65` |
| 6 | `env_names` element grammar `{0,127}` | `environmentNamePattern` `{0,127}` → `{0,128}` |
| 7 | `env_literals` `[0..64]` | `len(envLiterals) > 64` → `65` |
| 8 | `env_literals` value ≤ 4,096 bytes | `len(text) > 4096` → `4097` (the `env_literals` occurrence) |
| 9 | `task_element_id` 1–128 bytes | `requirePrintableByteBoundedString(object,"task_element_id",1,128)` → `129` |
| 10 | `task_element_id` printable non-control | `if unicode.IsControl(character)` → `if false && …` |
| 11 | Board Goal `goal_id` 1–128 characters | `requireBoundedString(object,"goal_id",1,128)` → `129` |

Note: widening `boardLogicalIDPattern` `{0,127}` → `{0,128}` also survives, but
that one is an **equivalent mutant** — `logical_id` length is independently
enforced by `requireBoundedString(…,1,128)`, so no over-long value is admitted.
It is excluded from this list.

